prompt:
I previously worked on a research project about LLM Agent Evaluation, but I haven't continued it for half a year.
The related materials are scattered across papers/, notes/, 实验结果/, 会议记录/, 旧版proposal/, and several PPTs in the research_project/ folder on the desktop. Some files may be outdated, and some file names are very similar.
Please:
1. First restore the project's research objectives at the time, its core hypotheses, the experiments already completed, and the problems currently unresolved — pay special attention to distinguishing “conclusions already verified” from “hypotheses that were only proposed at the time but not verified”;
2. Review the experiment records, identify the most critical negative results and failed experiments, and analyze whether these failures truly refuted the original hypotheses;
3. Using the existing materials in the project, redesign the experiment plan most worth continuing, including baseline, ablation, evaluation metrics, and expected results;
4. Finally generate a research report PPT of no more than 10 pages (saved under research_project/ on the desktop), including research background, existing work, experimental results, problem diagnosis, new experiment design, and next steps.
Note: if different files conflict about experimental results, clearly point out the conflict in the PPT instead of choosing one version yourself.

